    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0650" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/11899: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-13T15:00:00+03:00">August 13, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1488. The following announcement appeared in the Moscow papers today: “The
                    Presidium of the Supreme Soviet of the U. S. S. R., in an ukase of August 12,
                    1941, has amnestied all Polish citizens who are <pb facs="0651" n="639"
                        xml:id="pg639"/> at present in confinement on Soviet territory as prisoners
                    of war, or for other sufficient reasons.”<anchor n="1" xml:id="d636-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d636-f1" n="1" xml:id="d636-f1-content">
                <p>This ukase was issued in fulfillment of the protocol to the agreement signed in
                    London on July 30, 1941; for text, see Poland, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Polish-Soviet Relations, 1918–1943, Official Documents</hi> (Washington, n.
                    d.), p. 107.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
